WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.097
The takeaway is that recasting uncertainty as the
problem of compressing training data

00:00:05.177 --> 00:00:10.394
into a learned codebook gives a single
deterministic network a genuine sense of distance

00:00:10.474 --> 00:00:11.718
from what it has seen,

00:00:11.798 --> 00:00:15.992
letting it match or beat expensive ensembles at a
fraction of the cost.

00:00:16.072 --> 00:00:20.085
Because the notion of distance is statistical
rather than geometric,

00:00:20.165 --> 00:00:21.349
DAB offers a unified,

00:00:21.429 --> 00:00:26.887
Gaussian-Process-like view of uncertainty that
works for both classification and regression,

00:00:26.967 --> 00:00:30.980
and can even be attached after the fact to large
pre-trained models.
